    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI considered it during writing of 'mini.icons', but decided to use default links to built-in groups for at least these reasons:\r\n- Having defined [linked built-in groups](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7c00ea1a6b35332746e1a2fa768e26c5fa9c3589/lua/mini/icons.lua#L1947-L1955) is most certainly more common in color schemes than having set terminal colors. Yes, it does not always result in the specified hues, but at least most of them (I'd say 6 out of 9) are usually different, which is good enough.\r\n- Having explicit definition instead of default linking would require an extra autocommand for `ColorScheme` event to keep highlight groups defined. This results in extra code and tests.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
